WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.687
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:05.987 --> 00:00:09.791
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.091 --> 00:00:16.981
Unit twenty-two: Agriculture and Rural News. Today you will link causes and results with 'lead to' and 'result in'.

4
00:00:17.281 --> 00:00:19.922
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:24.065
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:26.150
Agriculture.

7
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.102
Agriculture means the science and practice of farming.

8
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.879
Agriculture feeds the whole country.

9
00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:36.020
Your turn. Say: Agriculture.

10
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:40.042
Agriculture.

11
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:41.575
Farmer.

12
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:46.115
Farmer means a person who grows crops or raises animals.

13
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.786
The farmer planted rice in June.

14
00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:52.082
Your turn. Say: Farmer.

15
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:55.725
Farmer.

16
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:57.403
Harvest.

17
00:00:58.417 --> 00:01:00.881
Harvest means the gathering of ripe crops.

18
00:01:01.483 --> 00:01:03.587
The harvest was larger than last year.

19
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:06.859
Your turn. Say: Harvest.

20
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.573
Harvest.

21
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:12.120
Rice.

22
00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:17.241
Rice means a grain grown in flooded fields and eaten daily by millions.

23
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.977
Rice is Cambodia's main crop.

24
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:23.317
Your turn. Say: Rice.

25
00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:27.133
Rice.

26
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:28.675
Drought.

27
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:32.519
Drought means a long period with very little rain.

28
00:01:33.117 --> 00:01:35.093
Drought can lead to a poor harvest.

29
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:37.941
Your turn. Say: Drought.

30
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.627
Drought.

31
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:43.477
Irrigation.

32
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:48.410
Irrigation means supplying water to crops through channels or pipes.

33
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.724
Irrigation protects the rice from dry weather.

34
00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:54.795
Your turn. Say: Irrigation.

35
00:01:57.633 --> 00:01:58.692
Irrigation.

36
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.648
Market price.

37
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.950
Market price means the price at which goods are sold at present.

38
00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.060
The market price of rice fell in July.

39
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.384
Your turn. Say: Market price.

40
00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:15.501
Market price.

41
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.239
Rural.

42
00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.540
Rural means connected with the countryside.

43
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.370
Rural families depend on farming.

44
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:26.403
Your turn. Say: Rural.

45
00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.186
Rural.

46
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.430
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:41.813
Visal, the news says 'Drought could lead to a poor harvest and result in higher prices.' What do 'lead to' and 'result in' do?

48
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:49.331
They connect a cause with its effect. 'Drought leads to a poor harvest' means the drought is the cause.

49
00:02:50.417 --> 00:02:52.370
Which preposition comes after?

50
00:02:53.483 --> 00:03:03.891
Both take a noun: lead to a shortage, result in higher prices. With 'result from' the order reverses: higher prices result from drought.

51
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.354
Why does this matter to people in cities?

52
00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:15.349
Because a poor harvest in rural areas changes the market price, so city families pay more for rice.

53
00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.954
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.817 --> 00:03:23.521
Grammar focus: Cause and result: lead to and result in and result from.

55
00:03:23.821 --> 00:03:24.950
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.661
Drought can lead to a poor harvest.

57
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:30.933
Poor irrigation results in lower yields.

58
00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:34.281
Higher prices result from a poor harvest.

59
00:03:35.233 --> 00:03:44.181
Cause + lead to / result in + effect. For 'result from', put the effect first: higher prices result from drought. Do not say 'result to'.

60
00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:48.602
Be careful! Don't say: Drought results to a poor harvest.

61
00:03:50.567 --> 00:03:52.926
Say: Drought results in a poor harvest.

62
00:03:53.226 --> 00:03:55.446
Say 'result in', not 'result to'.

63
00:03:56.233 --> 00:03:58.828
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:00.994
From Field to Market.

65
00:04:01.294 --> 00:04:05.128
Agriculture news explains how rural life affects the whole country.

66
00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:11.941
A long drought can lead to a poor harvest, and a poor harvest may result in a high market price for rice.

67
00:04:12.933 --> 00:04:17.394
Irrigation helps farmers, because reliable water leads to steadier crops.

68
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:22.803
City shoppers then pay less, which shows how rural events reach every table.

69
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:27.239
Farmers therefore deserve attention in the daily news.

70
00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:32.312
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.068
Drought can blank a poor harvest.

72
00:04:35.368 --> 00:04:39.625
A, lead to. B, result of. C, cause to.

73
00:04:43.167 --> 00:04:45.584
The answer is A: lead to.

74
00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:49.644
Supplying water to crops through channels is blank.

75
00:04:49.944 --> 00:04:53.353
A, irrigation. B, harvest. C, rural.

76
00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.213
The answer is A: irrigation.

77
00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.406
The price at which goods are sold now is the blank price.

78
00:05:03.706 --> 00:05:06.872
A, market. B, rural. C, farm.

79
00:05:10.433 --> 00:05:12.549
The answer is A: market.

80
00:05:13.683 --> 00:05:15.381
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:23.584
A, Poor rain results to a bad harvest.. B, Poor rain results in a bad harvest.. C, Poor rain result a bad harvest..

82
00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:30.584
The answer is B: Poor rain results in a bad harvest..

83
00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.876
According to the reading, reliable water leads to steadier…

84
00:05:35.176 --> 00:05:38.968
A, crops. B, cities. C, prices only.

85
00:05:42.533 --> 00:05:44.324
The answer is A: crops.

86
00:05:45.533 --> 00:05:48.720
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:52.314
How does agriculture news affect people in cities?

88
00:06:01.117 --> 00:06:02.663
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:02.963 --> 00:06:24.499
Agriculture news affects people in cities because food prices depend on farming. If a drought leads to a poor rice harvest, shops may charge more, and families have to spend more money. Good news about irrigation or a large harvest can keep prices steady. So city people should care about rural news too.

90
00:06:24.799 --> 00:06:26.369
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:27.283 --> 00:06:33.721
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and cause and result: lead to and result in and result from.

92
00:06:34.021 --> 00:06:38.914
Today's value is food responsibility. Value food and the people who produce it.

93
00:06:39.214 --> 00:06:42.458
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:42.758 --> 00:06:45.724
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

